---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout page="index">
<main id="main-content">
  <section
    id="home"
    class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          Really Good Engineering Solutions
        </p>
        <h1>
          Practical technology advice. Help getting it done.
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          RGE Solutions helps leaders and teams solve technology problems, improve operations, and make better spending decisions. We assess what is working, identify what needs to change, and help put the plan into practice.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a
            href="/contact"
            class="button primary">
            Let’s Talk
          </a>
          <a
            href="#services"
            class="button secondary">
            View Services
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel">
  <article class="signal-card large">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-engineering-clarity-822x500.webp"
      alt=""
      width="822"
      height="500"
      loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async" />
    <div class="signal-content">
      <span class="signal-label">
        Focus
      </span>
      <strong>
        A practical plan
      </strong>
      <p>
        Bring systems, security, data, vendors, and teams together in a plan people can put to work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-cloud-and-infrastructure-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      Cloud and infrastructure
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-cybersecurity-and-risk-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      Cybersecurity and risk
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-vendor-and-spend-control-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      Vendor and spend control
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-ai-and-data-readiness-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      AI and data readiness
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="work"
    class="section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">
        What RGE does
      </p>
      <h2>
        Turn technology plans into working improvements.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-stack">
      <p>
        We look at systems, teams, vendors, costs, and risks to understand what is working and what is getting in the way.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then we help leaders decide what to change and support the work—from improving systems and security to bringing businesses together or getting a troubled program back on track.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="services"
    class="section service-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Services
      </p>
      <h2>
        Help with the technology decisions and problems facing your business.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="service-grid">
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          01
        </span>
        <h3>
          Technology Teams &amp; Operations
        </h3>
        <p>
          Clarify responsibilities, improve how work gets done, and give teams the support they need.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          02
        </span>
        <h3>
          Infrastructure &amp; Cloud
        </h3>
        <p>
          Make systems more reliable, address outdated technology, and choose the right mix of cloud and on-site systems for the business.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          03
        </span>
        <h3>
          Cybersecurity &amp; Compliance
        </h3>
        <p>
          Understand security risks, improve safeguards, and help teams prepare for applicable requirements such as NIST, CMMC, HIPAA, HITECH, and PCI DSS.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          04
        </span>
        <h3>
          Vendors &amp; Technology Costs
        </h3>
        <p>
          Find duplicate tools, unused services, and contracts that no longer meet the organization’s needs. Make spending and renewals easier to manage.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          05
        </span>
        <h3>
          AI, Data &amp; Automation
        </h3>
        <p>
          Identify useful applications for AI and automation. Check whether the data, systems, safeguards, and working practices are ready to support them.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          06
        </span>
        <h3>
          Program Recovery &amp; Delivery
        </h3>
        <p>
          Get stalled programs moving with clear priorities, named responsibilities, and regular progress reviews.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="approach"
    class="section approach-section">
    <div class="section-heading narrow">
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Approach
      </p>
      <h2>
        Understand the problem. Make a plan. Follow through.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Understand the problem
        </h3>
        <p>
          Listen to the people doing the work, review the systems, and check the facts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Set priorities
        </h3>
        <p>
          Agree on what matters most: reliable service, manageable risks, sensible spending, and progress on the work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Make a plan
        </h3>
        <p>
          Define the work, the cost, and who is responsible. Make sure the plan is realistic for the people carrying it out.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Put it into practice
        </h3>
        <p>
          Help teams carry out the plan, track progress, hold vendors accountable, and address problems as they arise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="proof"
    class="section proof-section">
    <div class="proof-card intro-proof">
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Selected leadership experience
      </p>
      <h2>
        Experience from Tim Gabaree’s technology leadership roles.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-card metric">
      <strong>
        $25M
      </strong>
      <p>
        Projected savings identified through modernization, analytics, and financial controls.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-card metric">
      <strong>
        $115M
      </strong>
      <p>
        At-risk federal program stabilized by restoring delivery and improving operations.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-card metric">
      <strong>
        100+
      </strong>
      <p>
        Sites supported through cloud, infrastructure, cybersecurity, and day-to-day technology operations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
<section class="section founder-section">
  <div class="founder-card founder-card-with-photo">
    <div class="founder-copy">
      <div class="founder-label">
        Founder-led consulting
      </div>
      <h2>
        Led by Tim Gabaree
      </h2>
      <p>
        RGE Solutions is led by Tim Gabaree, a CIO and technology executive with experience in infrastructure, cybersecurity, and operations across government, healthcare, defense, private equity-backed businesses, and mid-market organizations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tim brings people, technology, and business priorities together. His approach is practical: understand the problem, build on what works, and help people deliver.
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://timgabaree.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-link">
        Learn more about Tim Gabaree
        <span class="visually-hidden">
          — opens in a new tab
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="founder-photo-wrap">
      <img
        class="founder-photo"
        src="/media/profile-pic-tim-gabaree-900x1200.webp"
        alt="Tim Gabaree, founder of RGE Solutions"
        width="900"
        height="1200"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
  <section
    id="contact"
    class="section contact-section">
    <div class="contact-box">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">
          Contact
        </p>
        <h2>
          Let’s talk about your technology challenge.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Tell us what you need to improve, what is getting in the way, and where you could use help.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-actions">
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="button primary">
          Let’s Talk
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/rgesolutions"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button secondary">
          LinkedIn
          <span class="visually-hidden">
            — opens in a new tab
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Layout>
